# Images are split by PROVENANCE, not by format, because the three kinds
# carry different rights and only two of them may be published. This
# repository is public: committing an image here publishes it to the
# whole internet as a standalone downloadable file.
#
# This directory root — LICENSED STOCK. Not committed. A stock licence is
# granted to you, not to everyone who clones this, and redistributing the
# image as a standalone file is the thing those licences most reliably
# forbid. Keep them here, upload them, leave them out of git.
#
# owned/ — photographs the project owner holds full rights to (their own
# camera, or bought outright). Committed: no third party's permission is
# needed to publish them.
#
# generated/ — AI-generated originals produced for this project. Also
# committed, for the same reason: nobody else's rights attach.
#
# All three share one filename namespace at upload time, in the order
# generated -> owned -> root, so the more specific/deliberate a file is,
# the more it wins: a real photograph beats generated artwork of the same
# name, and anything you put in the root beats both
# (see ../scripts/upload-images.mjs).
#
# `*` matches at every depth, so re-including a directory is not enough on
# its own — the `/**` lines are what actually let the files inside through.
*
!.gitignore
!README.md
!owned/
!owned/**
!generated/
!generated/**
